{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Algebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.JonesNormalForm"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.markov_trace_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.markov_trace_unique","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L215-L228","doc":"**Uniqueness of the Markov trace (Ocneanu 1985; Jones 1987), sorry-free.**\nTwo `MarkovTrace`s on the same `HeckeAlgebra` with the same Markov parameter that both\nsatisfy the cross-level Markov property (M3) have the same trace.\n\nThe (M3) hypotheses are necessary, not decorative: without them the conclusion is false\n(`QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceClassNotUnique.markov_trace_unique_axiom_false`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.IsMarkov.genSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.IsMarkov.genSeq","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L207-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.IsMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.IsMarkov","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L200-L205","doc":"**The cross-level Markov property (M3)** for a `MarkovTrace`:\n`tr(x · σ_i) = z · tr(x)` whenever `x` lies in the subalgebra generated by the\ngenerators of index `< i`. This is the axiom the `MarkovTrace` class does not carry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.genSeq_adjoin_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.genSeq_adjoin_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L193-L198","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.genSeq_heckeFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.genSeq_heckeFamily","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L178-L191","doc":"The class relations make `genSeq` a `HeckeFamily` with quadratic `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.genSeq_image_Iio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.genSeq_image_Iio","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L168-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.genSeq_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.genSeq_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L165-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.genSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.genSeq","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L160-L163","doc":"The generators as an `ℕ`-indexed family: `genSeq k = σ_k` for `k < n - 1`, and `0`\npast the top (never used there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_gen_mul_invGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_gen_mul_invGen","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L104-L123","doc":"**Trace of a generator times an inverse generator**:\n`tr_M(σ_i · σ_j⁻¹) = z² − (q − q⁻¹)·z` for `i < j`.\n\nThe Hecke quadratic relation gives `σ_j⁻¹ = σ_j − (q − q⁻¹)·1`\n(`HeckeAlgebra.inv_formula`), so writing `σ_j⁻¹` in that form and using\n`R`-linearity of the trace:\n\n  `tr_M(σ_i · (σ_j − (q−q⁻¹)·1))\n    = tr_M(σ_i·σ_j) − (q−q⁻¹)·tr_M(σ_i)\n    = z² − (q−q⁻¹)·z`\n\nby `trace_prod_gen` (`i < j`) and `trace_gen`.  This is the **denominator**\n`tr_M(T_β)` of the Pauli-full-shell knot operator `F(τ,N)` in\n`cor:spectral-decomposition-qvalue`, whose decay operator is\n`T_β = σ_0 · σ_1⁻¹` (`i = 0`, `j = 1`).  Bean `qou-xq3f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_idempotent_sandwich'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_idempotent_sandwich'","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L98-L102","doc":"The mirror form: `tr_M(e · x · e) = tr_M(x · e)` for an idempotent `e`.\nSame derivation via cyclicity applied to the leading factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_idempotent_sandwich","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_idempotent_sandwich","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L85-L96","doc":"**Idempotent-sandwich collapse.** For an idempotent `e` (`e * e = e`),\n`tr_M(e · x · e) = tr_M(e · x)`.  Derived purely from the cyclicity axiom\n(M2) and idempotency: `tr(e·x·e) = tr(e·(e·x)) = tr((e·e)·x) = tr(e·x)`.\n\nThis is the structural simplification behind the **Pauli-full-shell** case of\nthe knot operator `F(τ, N)` in `cor:spectral-decomposition-qvalue`, whose\nnumerator is `|tr_M(e_{(1³)} · τ · T_β · e_{(1³)})|` with `e_{(1³)}` the\nalternating Young idempotent: the outer `e` sandwich collapses, so the\nnumerator equals `|tr_M(e_{(1³)} · τ · T_β)|`.  Bean `qou-xq3f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_pair","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L77-L83","doc":"Pair-of-generators trace formula:\n    tr_M(σ_i · σ_j) = z²  for i < j\n[leitner2026] `prop:markov-pair-z2` — direct two-step Markov peel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_generator","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The Markov trace value of a Hecke generator: tr_M(σ_i) = z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_prod_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_prod_gen","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L61-L61","doc":"(M3 / pair product) tr_M(σ_i · σ_j) = z² when i < j.\nFollows from two consecutive Markov peels: σ_j is top-indexed,\none peel gives z · tr_{n-1}(σ_i); σ_i lives in H_{n-1} so the\nsecond peel gives z · z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace_gen","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L56-L56","doc":"(M3 / generator value) tr_M(σ_i) = z for every generator.\nThis is the key consequence of the full Markov axiom\n`tr_M^{H_n}(x · σ_{n-1}) = z · tr_M^{H_{n-1}}(x)` applied at\nlevel n with x = 1 ∈ H_{n-1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.z_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.z_param","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The Markov parameter z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}). Stored as a\nfield rather than a definition because q^{1/2} requires choosing\na square root extension of R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L47-L47","doc":"(M2) Cyclicity: trace(x · y) = trace(y · x). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.normalised","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L45-L45","doc":"(M1) Normalisation: tr_M(1) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.trace","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The trace as an R-linear map A → R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","kind":"class","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L31-L62","doc":"Markov trace structure on `H_n(q)`. Encodes the three Markov axioms\nplus the connection to the Markov parameter `z`.\n\nFor the chain `H_1 ⊂ H_2 ⊂ ...` the Markov axiom relates traces at\nadjacent levels; we capture this via a parameterised family of\ntraces and a coherence condition.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}